---
import ToolPage from '../../components/ToolPage.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Does the helper solve the puzzle?',
    a: 'By default it lists candidates for the selected cell without filling answers. The explicitly labeled Reveal button can search for one complete solution to a consistent entered grid; it does not establish uniqueness.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is "hidden single"?',
    a: 'A digit that can only go in one cell of a row, column, or box even though other cells show it as a candidate. The worked explanation distinguishes it from a naked single; the helper does not automatically detect hidden singles.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does it default to non-spoiler?',
    a: 'The helper shows candidates from the grid you typed, not from its own solution. You can opt into a full solve with the clearly-labeled Reveal button; NoCharge does not hide that button behind a second feature.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can it handle a 6×6 grid?',
    a: 'Yes. Choose the size; box shape changes between 3×2 (6×6) and 3×3 (9×9). The candidate logic is identical.',
  },
];
---

<ToolPage
  title="Sudoku pencil-mark helper"
  eyebrow="Candidates, not answers"
  description="Enter a 6×6 or 9×9 grid, inspect one cell's candidates, and learn the elimination rule. An optional full solve is clearly labeled; hidden singles are not automatically detected."
  path="/tools/sudoku-helper/"
  category="Learning"
  bottomLine="Type a 6×6 or 9×9 grid and select an empty cell to list the digits not already used in its row, column, or box. Candidates are not answers. Reveal is an explicit optional spoiler and does not prove the puzzle has only one solution."
  faqs={faqs}
  embedCode={`<iframe src="https://nocharge.net/tools/sudoku-helper/" width="400" height="640" title="NoCharge sudoku pencil-mark helper"></iframe>`}
  nextActions={[
    { href: '/games/mini-sudoku/', label: 'Play Mini Sudoku 6×6', note: 'The smaller grid the helper supports.' },
    { href: '/games/sudoku-9x9/', label: 'Play Sudoku 9×9', note: 'Full grid with pencil marks and check.' },
    { href: '/guides/sudoku-9x9/', label: 'Sudoku 9×9 guide', note: 'Methods and honest difficulty labels.' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="panel sudoku-helper" aria-labelledby="helper-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">One grid, your notes</p>
      <h2 id="helper-heading">Pencil marks without spoilers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="helper-controls">
      <label>Size
        <select data-helper-size aria-label="Grid size">
          <option value="6">6×6</option>
          <option value="9" selected>9×9</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-helper-clear>Clear grid</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-helper-reveal aria-pressed="false">Reveal full solution (spoiler)</button>
    </div>
    <div class="helper-grid" data-helper-grid></div>
    <p class="helper-status" data-helper-status aria-live="polite">Select a cell to see its candidates.</p>
    <div class="helper-note">
      <p>Click or tap to select a cell, then enter digits with the keyboard. The helper computes candidates from what you typed — if a digit is wrong, the candidates reflect your mistake, not a hidden answer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Fragment slot="how">
    <p>Select an empty square and enter board digits with the keyboard. Its candidates are the allowed digits, 1–6 or 1–9, minus every digit already present in the same row, column, or box. Boxes are three columns wide and either two or three rows high, depending on the grid size.</p>
    <h3>Worked example</h3>
    <p>On a 6×6 grid, suppose the selected cell's row uses 1 and 4, its column uses 2, and its box uses 1 and 3. The combined exclusions are 1, 2, 3, and 4, leaving candidates 5 and 6. If another square in that box is then filled with 5, only 6 remains for the selected square.</p>
    <p>One remaining candidate is a naked single. A hidden single is different: a digit has only one possible location across a whole row, column, or box. This helper lists one cell's candidates; it does not automatically search all units for hidden singles. Reveal is an explicit spoiler that tries backtracking to fill a complete grid consistent with the entered digits.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="limits">
    <ul>
      <li>Candidates describe your entries, not a hidden authoritative answer. A wrong but locally consistent entry can still lead to an incorrect or impossible puzzle.</li>
      <li>Reveal checks for contradictory digits and searches for a completion, but it does not prove uniqueness, grade difficulty, or explain each solving step.</li>
      <li>This is separate from the playable Sudoku games. It neither imports their boards nor changes their saved progress.</li>
      <li>Clicking selects a square; digit entry in this helper uses the keyboard. Clear, changing size, or reloading discards the typed grid; it is not saved.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolPage>

<script>
  const grid = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-helper-grid]');
  const sizeSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-helper-size]');
  const clearButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-helper-clear]');
  const revealButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-helper-reveal]');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-helper-status]');
  if (!grid || !status) throw new Error("missing helper elements");
  let size = 9;
  let values: number[][] = [];
  let selected = 0;

  const candidatesFor = (row: number, col: number) => {
    const used = new Set<number>();
    for (let i = 0; i < size; i += 1) {
      used.add(values[row]![i]!);
      used.add(values[i]![col]!);
    }
    const boxRows = size === 9 ? 3 : 2;
    const boxCols = size === 9 ? 3 : 3;
    const br = Math.floor(row / boxRows) * boxRows;
    const bc = Math.floor(col / boxCols) * boxCols;
    for (let r = br; r < br + boxRows; r += 1) {
      for (let c = bc; c < bc + boxCols; c += 1) used.add(values[r]![c]!);
    }
    return [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9].slice(0, size).filter((digit) => !used.has(digit));
  };

  const render = () => {
    const hadGridFocus = grid.contains(document.activeElement);
    grid.replaceChildren();
    grid.style.gridTemplateColumns = `repeat(${size}, 1fr)`;
    for (let index = 0; index < size * size; index += 1) {
      const row = Math.floor(index / size);
      const col = index % size;
      const button = document.createElement('button');
      button.type = 'button';
      button.className = 'helper-cell';
      if (row % (size === 9 ? 3 : 2) === 0) button.classList.add('is-box-top');
      if (col % 3 === 0) button.classList.add('is-box-left');
      if (index === selected) button.classList.add('is-selected');
      const value = values[row]![col]!;
      if (value) {
        button.textContent = String(value);
        button.setAttribute('aria-label', `Row ${row + 1}, column ${col + 1}: ${value}`);
      } else {
        button.setAttribute('aria-label', `Row ${row + 1}, column ${col + 1}, empty`);
      }
      button.addEventListener('click', () => { selected = index; render(); });
      grid.append(button);
    }
    if (hadGridFocus) {
      grid.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button')[selected]?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
    }
    if (status) {
      const row = Math.floor(selected / size);
      const col = selected % size;
      if (values[row]![col]) {
        status.textContent = 'Selected cell already has a digit. Clear it to see candidates.';
        return;
      }
      const candidates = candidatesFor(row, col);
      if (candidates.length === 0) {
        status.textContent = 'No candidates: the row, column, or box already uses every digit.';
        return;
      }
      status.textContent = `Candidates for row ${row + 1}, column ${col + 1}: ${candidates.join(', ')}.`;
    }
  };

  const rebuild = () => {
    values = Array.from({ length: size }, () => Array.from({ length: size }, () => 0));
    selected = 0;
    render();
  };

  sizeSelect?.addEventListener('change', () => {
    size = Number(sizeSelect.value);
    rebuild();
  });
  clearButton?.addEventListener('click', rebuild);
  revealButton?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    // Labeled spoiler: solve the typed grid with a simple backtracker and
    // fill it if a solution exists. No claim about uniqueness or game state.
    if (!status) return;
    const input = values.map((row) => row.slice());
    // Backtracking must not treat a fully filled but contradictory grid as solved.
    for (let row = 0; row < size; row += 1) {
      for (let col = 0; col < size; col += 1) {
        const digit = input[row]![col]!;
        if (digit === 0) continue;
        const boxRows = size === 9 ? 3 : 2;
        const conflict = input.some((cells, r) => cells.some((value, c) =>
          (r !== row || c !== col) && value === digit && (
            r === row || c === col || (
              Math.floor(r / boxRows) === Math.floor(row / boxRows) &&
              Math.floor(c / 3) === Math.floor(col / 3)
            )
          )
        ));
        if (!Number.isInteger(digit) || digit < 1 || digit > size || conflict) {
          status.textContent = 'The entered grid contains conflicting digits. Correct them before using Reveal.';
          return;
        }
      }
    }
    const solve = (): boolean => {
      let best: [number, number, number[]] | null = null;
      for (let r = 0; r < size; r += 1) {
        for (let c = 0; c < size; c += 1) {
          if (input[r]![c] !== 0) continue;
          const options = candidatesFor(r, c).filter((digit) => {
            // candidatesFor reads `values`; evaluate against input locally.
            const used = new Set<number>();
            for (let i = 0; i < size; i += 1) { used.add(input[r]![i]!); used.add(input[i]![c]!); }
            const br = Math.floor(r / (size === 9 ? 3 : 2)) * (size === 9 ? 3 : 2);
            const bc = Math.floor(c / 3) * 3;
            for (let y = br; y < br + (size === 9 ? 3 : 2); y += 1) for (let x = bc; x < bc + 3; x += 1) used.add(input[y]![x]!);
            return !used.has(digit);
          });
          if (options.length === 0) return false;
          if (best === null || options.length < best[2].length) best = [r, c, options];
        }
      }
      if (best === null) return true;
      for (const digit of best[2]) {
        input[best[0]]![best[1]] = digit;
        if (solve()) return true;
        input[best[0]]![best[1]] = 0;
      }
      return false;
    };
    const solved = solve();
    if (!solved) {
      status.textContent = 'No complete grid exists for what you typed — check for a duplicate digit.';
      return;
    }
    values = input.map((row) => row.slice());
    revealButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
    render();
    status.textContent = 'Full solution filled from the typed grid. This is the spoiler button you chose.';
  });

  grid?.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
    if (/^[1-9]$/.test(event.key) && Number(event.key) <= size) {
      const row = Math.floor(selected / size);
      const col = selected % size;
      values[row]![col] = Number(event.key);
      event.preventDefault();
      render();
    } else if (event.key === 'Backspace' || event.key === '0') {
      const row = Math.floor(selected / size);
      const col = selected % size;
      values[row]![col] = 0;
      event.preventDefault();
      render();
    } else if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') {
      selected = (selected + 1) % (size * size);
      render();
    } else if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') {
      selected = (selected + size * size - 1) % (size * size);
      render();
    } else if (event.key === 'ArrowDown') {
      selected = (selected + size) % (size * size);
      render();
    } else if (event.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      selected = (selected + size * size - size) % (size * size);
      render();
    }
  });

  rebuild();
</script>

<style is:global>
  .sudoku-helper {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .sudoku-helper > div:first-child {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .helper-controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .helper-controls label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .helper-controls select {
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--panel-2);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .helper-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    width: min(100%, 24rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    border: 2px solid #4a5852;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .helper-cell {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--panel-2);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 4vw, 1.2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .helper-cell.is-box-top {
    border-top: 2px solid #4a5852;
  }

  .helper-cell.is-box-left {
    border-left: 2px solid #4a5852;
  }

  .helper-cell.is-selected {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent-strong);
    outline-offset: -2px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, var(--panel-2));
  }

  .helper-status {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    min-height: 1.3rem;
  }

  .helper-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
